Keep agent status busy during delegated work

An idle parent or a finished subagent does not mean the whole task has
finished. Track Claude subagents per session and aggregate Codex thread
statuses so outstanding work continues to show as processing.

Restore loaded Codex thread states after monitor reconnects and treat
user input and approval waits as idle. Cover overlapping agents, session
shutdown, and reconnect snapshots with regression tests. Exercise real
Claude and Codex subagents with recorded model responses and FIFO gates
so status checks observe controlled periods of outstanding work.

Keep delegated messages and completed tool-step counts in Codex cache
keys, and normalize Claude subagent metadata so delegation replays
without collisions or per-run cache misses.

Require repeated integration test runs without automatic retries and
runtime checks so new coverage does not hide flakes or excessive delays.
